# Two recipients, two grants, one ciphertext. Anna decrypts with the key behind
# the public key she published on her own name; she never registered with
# NextKey. The owner takes the identical path — there is no owner-only branch
# and no master key, which is why "we cannot read your secrets" is a statement
# about the code rather than a promise about our conduct.
